<article class="env-remark" id="07VL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07VL">Remark <span data-tag="07VL">30.22.2</span>.</a> A consequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/07VK" data-tag="07VK">30.22.1</a> is that there exists a finite complex of finite projective $A$-modules $M^\bullet $ such that we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  H^ i(X_{A'}, \mathcal{F}_{A'}) = H^ i(M^\bullet \otimes _ A A')  \]
</div>
  <p> functorially in $A'$. The condition that $\mathcal{F}$ is flat over $A$ is essential, see <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Hartshorne">Hartshorne</a>]</span>. </p>
</article>